A||||6||loren||timing marks v6||||1||
Z||000000||loren||02-21-2001||06:40 PM||||i am having trouble getting my engine timed correctly. i have read page 52 of the haynes manual and have located the stationary timing plate and see the 8 marks on it but cannot see the mark (or marks) on the crank pulley. is there more than one mark on the pulley ?<BR>the engine is running well but with a little miss at idle speed so i guess that i am close<BR>to original timing.  i just replaced the pickup coil and probably got her a wee bit out of time. btw i did put a jumper on the alcl connector.<BR>any and all information would be appreciated.<P>loren  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||c m west||02-21-2001||08:21 PM||||it can be problematic getting a timing light in the passenger side area. I would suggest cleaning the dampener so that you can see the timing mark - and there is only one.<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DavidHenshaw||02-21-2001||08:23 PM||||There is only one mark on the pulley and when it aligns with the TDC mark on the stationary plate it means the number one piston is at TDC (top dead center)<P>Are you using a timing light?  If you are using a timing light then you should only be able to see one timing mark on each revolution of the pully as the engine runs.<BR>You see the mark for a split second when it is illuminated by the very short burst of light from the timing light.<P>If you are not using a timing light then the best way to time the engine IMHO is to just hand turn the distributor cap until the engine sounds best.<P>Lastly, if you are using a light be sure to follow the Haynes book directions; ie, warm engine, transmission in gear, etc. etc.    <P><BR>Dave<P>86 GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||02-21-2001||09:08 PM||||All the 2.8's that I have at this time (or ever) have 3 marks on the dampner. You want to use the WIDEST one. Clean the area around it and the groove and mark it with something you can see. (I use white model paint)<BR>Then set your timing according with the book or deck lid decal.||||reg||1
Z||000004||c m west||02-21-2001||09:38 PM||||DO NOT TURN THE DISTRIBUTOR BY HAND!!!! -  unless you want your hair to stand up for a week - us something plastic to spin it - i.e. non-conductive<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||DavidHenshaw||02-22-2001||02:17 AM||||Guess I should have warned to wear gloves or something. I wear heavy gloves if I do it. It only takes one jolt to learn that lesson real good.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
